al reports on file etc.&nbsp;Boundary &amp; parcel history
2. The boundary survey you sent appears to cover two parcels: 1621 and 16=
15 Clermont Rd, but not the small southeastern area that the Durham GIS s=
hows as part of 1621 and outside the old landfill (circled in red in the =
map below). Was this one tract that was divided, with extra land recombin=
ed in? Can you point me to the recorded plats and deeds showing that hist=
ory if so?
3. Is the south-east corner (the part outside the landfill footprint) con=
firmed clean of waste in your records?Zoning &amp; subdivision potential
4. What does the RS-10 zoning allow by-right on this specific parcel, giv=
en the site constraints?
5. Can this 9.4-ac tract be split as a minor subdivision (=E2=89=A43 lots=
, plat-only under NCGS 160D-802(c))? Specifically, if a portion near Cler=
mont Rd is clear of the landfill footprint, could I create two single-fam=
ily RS-10 lots there? Would conventional standards (10,000 sf / 75 ft wid=
th) fit, or would I need cluster-subdivision standards (5,000 sf / 40 ft)=
?
6. Does each potential lot have enough Clermont Rd frontage and legal acc=
ess or would I have to build out the road?Flood / buffer / wetland
7. Does the AE flood area include a mapped regulatory floodway (not just =
floodplain)?
8. What's the Base Flood Elevation here, and roughly how much fill would =
a buildable pad need (2 ft above BFE)?
9. Is the rear stream perennial or intermittent i.e., is the buffer 100 f=
t or 50 ft? (You mentioned 110'.)
10. Has the wetland (3.06 ac PFO) been delineated, or would I need a deli=
neation + Army Corps 404 sign-off?Process, cost &amp; restrictions
11. Does the City require NCDEQ Solid Waste sign-off before issuing a bui=
lding permit on this parcel and is there a documented compaction/geotech =
requirement from Building &amp; Safety?
12. Are there any open code-enforcement actions, environmental violations=
, or liens on the property?
13. Roughly what impact fees would apply? (The parcel sits in Parks Zone =
1, Open Space 1C, Streets Zone 4, so I would like the cost picture.)=E2=80=
=8BThis was the previous info you provided:To give a summary, this proper=
ty was used as an unpermitted solid waste disposal site until it was clos=
ed by the State in 1991. Please see attached. Any additional regulations =
on development may be in the hands of the NC Dept. of Waste Management. A=
dditionally, Building &amp; Safety may have a say in how things can be bu=
ilt on the ground since there are likely compaction considerations with t=
he landfill.Much of the property is also in flood areas, and there is als=
o a 110' riparian buffer to the rear of the property.Lastly, there is a c=
hance you would need to build out the road to get street access and utili=
ties to the property.Let me know if you would like me to send over the fu=
ll information.
